{
  "reference_answer": "Honestly, not as much as I'd like to. I can cook — I just don't get much joy out of it when I'm cooking only for myself. It feels like a chore: chopping, waiting, then ten minutes of eating and a sink full of dishes. The one time I genuinely enjoy it is when there's company. If a friend comes over, suddenly it's worth the effort — I'll actually plan a proper meal and take my time with it. So for me it's less about the cooking itself and more about who's at the table. Left to my own devices, I'd happily live on toast and fruit.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "独立主线：以“独处时做饭像家务、有人一起吃才值得”为唯一理由，回答是否喜欢做饭；示例不代表用户经历。",
  "takeaway_expressions": [
    {
      "expression": "not as much as I'd like to",
      "meaning_zh": "没有我希望的那么喜欢/那么多",
      "why_useful": "回答喜好类问题时自然留有余地，比直接说 no 更口语、更有层次",
      "example": "Do I read these days? Not as much as I'd like to, honestly.",
      "usage_note": "常放句首，后面可自然接原因"
    },
    {
      "expression": "it feels like a chore",
      "meaning_zh": "感觉像一件不得不做的杂活",
      "why_useful": "高频表达，用来解释为什么某件事缺乏乐趣，适用于家务、工作、日常任务",
      "example": "Grocery shopping on a Sunday feels like a chore to me.",
      "usage_note": "chore 是可数名词，前面常加 a"
    },
    {
      "expression": "left to my own devices",
      "meaning_zh": "如果由我自己决定/没人管我的话",
      "why_useful": "地道习语，用来说明个人习惯或真实选择，适合对比“有人陪”和“独自”的场景",
      "example": "Left to my own devices, I'd probably skip breakfast entirely.",
      "usage_note": "常放句首，后接 would 或一般现在时"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "reference_answer": "I enjoy it, but only under a very specific condition — I have to be cooking something I've never made before. If it's a dish I already know by heart, my brain checks out and it just feels like assembly work. So I rarely repeat recipes. Last month I tried making hand-pulled noodles, and they came out thick and lumpy, nothing like the real thing, but I was completely absorbed for two hours. That's the part I actually enjoy: the problem-solving. Once I've cracked a dish, the fun is basically over, which is why my cooking is a bit inconsistent. It's not really about eating — it's about having something to figure out.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "独立主线：只在新菜谱、需要解决新问题时才享受做饭，重复做熟悉的菜就失去兴趣；示例不代表用户经历。",
  "takeaway_expressions": [
    {
      "expression": "under a very specific condition",
